### EduHub Monorepo Overview

- **Project**: EduHub — educational platform for course management, registration, and learning. Repo: [eduhub/eduhub](https://github.com/eduhub/eduhub)
- **Monorepo**: Nx workspace with frontend and backend separation. Root configs: [package.json](mdc:package.json), [pnpm-workspace.yaml](mdc:pnpm-workspace.yaml), [nx.json](mdc:frontend-nx/nx.json)
- **Frontend**: Next.js app in `frontend-nx/apps/edu-hub` with TypeScript, Material-UI, GraphQL, i18n. Components organized by feature in [frontend-nx/apps/edu-hub/components/](mdc:frontend-nx/apps/edu-hub/components/)
- **Backend**: Hasura GraphQL API with PostgreSQL. Schema and migrations in [backend/migrations/](mdc:backend/migrations/), metadata in [backend/metadata/](mdc:backend/metadata/)
- **Authentication**: Keycloak integration with SSO support. Configuration in [keycloak/](mdc:keycloak/)
- **Functions**: Serverless functions for email, notifications, and integrations in [functions/](mdc:functions/)

### Package Management Strategy

- **Frontend**: Uses **pnpm workspace** for optimal performance, disk space efficiency, and dependency management
- **Functions**: Individual **npm packages** for Google Cloud Functions deployment compatibility
- **Root**: pnpm workspace coordinator with [pnpm-workspace.yaml](mdc:pnpm-workspace.yaml)
- **Lockfiles**: `pnpm-lock.yaml` (root), individual `package-lock.json` files for functions
- **IMPORTANT**: Always run `pnpm install` from root directory only - never from `frontend-nx/` to avoid duplicate lock files

### Apps

- **frontend-nx/apps/edu-hub**: Main Next.js application (UI, components, pages, GraphQL integration, i18n)
- **frontend-nx/apps/rent-a-scientist**: Secondary application for scientist booking platform

### Key Directories

- **frontend-nx/apps/edu-hub/components/**: Feature-oriented component organization
  - `common/`: Shared reusable components (dialogs, TableGrid, buttons)
  - `inputs/`: Form input components (CreatableTagSelector, DropDownSelector, InputField)
  - `pages/`: Page-specific components organized by feature
- **frontend-nx/apps/edu-hub/locales/**: Internationalization files (German "Du" form required)
- **backend/migrations/**: Database schema migrations
- **backend/metadata/**: Hasura GraphQL metadata and permissions
- **functions/**: Serverless functions for backend operations

### Tech Stack

- **Frontend**: Next.js, React, TypeScript, Material-UI, Apollo GraphQL, next-translate
- **Backend**: Hasura GraphQL, PostgreSQL, Keycloak, Node.js/Python functions
- **Development**: Docker, Nx workspace, pnpm, Jest, ESLint, Prettier

### Development Environment Containers

When running locally with `docker-compose up`, the following containers are started:

- **eduhub** (frontend-nx): Next.js development server
  - Ports: 5000:4200 (edu-hub), 5001:4201 (rent-a-scientist)
  - Serves the main EduHub application and secondary rent-a-scientist app
- **python-functions**: Python serverless functions container
  - Ports: 42025:42025, 42026:42026
  - Handles API proxy, data processing, and Python-based cloud functions
- **db_hasura**: PostgreSQL database
  - Internal port: 5432
  - Stores all application data, user information, and course content
- **keycloak**: Authentication and identity management
  - Port: 28080:8080
  - Provides SSO, user authentication, and authorization services
- **node-functions**: Node.js serverless functions container
  - Ports: 42000-42024:42000-42024, 4001:4001
  - Handles email sending, file storage, certificates, and Node.js cloud functions
- **hasura**: GraphQL API engine
  - Port: 8080:8080
  - Provides GraphQL API layer over PostgreSQL with real-time subscriptions
- **frontend-nx**: Next.js applications container
  - Port: 5000:4200 (main), 5001:4201 (secondary)
  - Development server for both EduHub and Rent-a-Scientist applications

### Development Commands

```bash
# Frontend development
cd frontend-nx
pnpm dev                 # Start development server
pnpm build               # Build for production
pnpm test                # Run tests
pnpm lint                # Lint code

# Backend development
cd backend
docker-compose up        # Start Hasura and PostgreSQL
hasura console           # Open Hasura console

# Full stack
docker-compose up        # Start all services
```

### Component Architecture Principles

- **Feature-oriented organization**: Components grouped by business functionality
- **Component reuse**: Always check existing components before creating new ones
- **TypeScript-first**: Strict typing for all components and interfaces
- **GraphQL integration**: Apollo Client with proper error handling
- **Internationalization**: German "Du" form, English translations
- **Material-UI patterns**: Consistent design system usage

### Key Development Patterns

- **Component reuse**: Check `components/common/dialogs/`, `components/inputs/`, `components/common/` first
- **Error handling**: Use `ErrorMessageDialog`, `QuestionConfirmationDialog`, `NotificationSnackbar`
- **Data tables**: Use `TableGrid` component with pagination, sorting, filtering
- **Form inputs**: Use `CreatableTagSelector`, `DropDownSelector`, `InputField`
- **Translations**: Use `useTranslation` hook with snake_case keys
- **GraphQL**: Use `useAdminQuery`, `useRoleMutation` with proper error handling

### Essentials for every prompt

- **Tech stack**: Next.js, React, TypeScript, Material-UI, Apollo GraphQL, Hasura, PostgreSQL, Keycloak
- **Package management**: pnpm (frontend), npm (functions) - use correct manager for each context
- **Component organization**: Feature-oriented, check existing components first
- **Translations**: German "Du" form mandatory, English fallbacks
- **Error handling**: Comprehensive error boundaries and user feedback
- **Testing**: Jest, React Testing Library, component behavior testing

